@startuml sequence-ocr-job-lifecycle
!include elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: a client only declares (apply a spec, set desired = cancelled); the
'       facade's reconciler takes the transitions the job state machine allows,
'       runs report facts, and a provider's report or domain change is turned
'       into further declarations (follow-up jobs) — nothing calls retry/revoke.
' Kind: UML sequence diagram, proposal (IP-031 rev. 2). Scope: one OCR job
'       (#146) applied, run, reported; a blocked LCP follow-up that proceeds on
'       its own; cancel; a domain change observed. Omitted: auth, telemetry.
' Source: EvilFlowersCatalog IP-031 rev. 2; diagrams state-job, state-job-run
'         (2026-11-14).
' =============================================================================

title One OCR job, declaratively: apply, reconcile, facts, follow-ups, cancel (proposal rev. 2, 2026-11-14)

actor "Admin\nelvira-portal" as admin
participant "REST\n/api/v1/jobs" as api
participant "JobFacade\n+ Reconciler" as facade
participant "Definition\n(provider)" as definition
database "Ledger\nJob · JobRun" as ledger
queue "Redis db 7" as redis
participant "ocr worker" as worker

== apply (declare) ==
admin -[$accent_msg()]> api : <b>POST /api/v1/jobs</b>\n{kind: files.ocr, subject_id, spec: {redo: false}}
api -> facade : apply(kind, subject, spec, desired = completed)
facade -> definition : spec model validates spec
facade -> ledger : upsert Job(kind, subject):\nspec, generation + 1, state pending
api --> admin : 201 {state: pending, generation: 1}
facade -[$accent_msg()]> facade : <b>reconcile(job)</b> (on commit)
facade -> definition : check(subject, spec) → ok
facade -> ledger : JobRun(queued); Job: queued,\nobserved_generation = generation
facade -> definition : dispatch(run)
definition -> redis : send_task(task_id = run id)

== facts ==
redis -> worker : consume
worker -> redis : task-received · task-started
redis -> facade : events (via celery_event_handler)
facade -> ledger : run: started → Job: running

== report → follow-ups are declared too ==
worker -[$accent_msg()]> api : <b>PUT /api/v1/jobs/runs/{run}/report</b>\n{status: done, output, pages}
api -> facade : report(run, payload)
facade -> definition : on_report(subject, payload)\n→ file replaced, checksum cleared
definition -> facade : apply(readium.encrypt, subject,\n{reencrypt: true}, cause = job)
facade -> definition : check(…) → refused: 2 active loans
facade -> ledger : child Job: blocked (reason: active loans)
worker -> redis : task-succeeded
redis -> facade : event (via celery_event_handler)
facade -> ledger : run: succeeded → Job: succeeded

== later: the blocked job proceeds by itself ==
facade -> facade : reconcile tick (beat)
facade -> definition : check(…) → ok (loans ended)
facade -> ledger : child JobRun(queued); child Job: queued
facade -> definition : dispatch(run) → lcpencrypt

== cancel (declare) ==
admin -> api : PATCH /api/v1/jobs/{id}\n{desired_state: cancelled}
api -> facade : patch(job, desired = cancelled)
facade -> facade : reconcile: queued → revoke\n(running → cancelling until the run ends)
facade -> redis : control.revoke(run id)
facade -> ledger : run: revoked · Job: cancelled

== domain change observed ==
definition -> facade : observe(subject) on EncryptedContent\nsaved (webhook: registered)
facade -> ledger : Job: succeeded (observed),\nlisted even if nobody applied it

caption The only client inputs are POST (apply a spec) and PATCH (change spec or desired state); retry = apply again (generation + 1).\nThe reconciler decides: dispatch, block (re-checked later), revoke. Runs and domain changes are facts that move the state machine.\nA provider's consequences (re-encrypt after OCR) are declarations through the same facade, never direct task sends.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · EvilFlowersCatalog · docs/diagrams/sequence-ocr-job-lifecycle.puml
@enduml
